/**
 * Why the naive baseline scores below zero.
 *
 * Not a fact about naive forecasting. The generator adds a trend of 0.005 per day to the
 * input, and its own AR(0.85) feedback multiplies anything persistent by 1/(1-0.85). The
 * series therefore climbs about 0.033 a day, and the two periods end up on different levels.
 * A day-of-year mean taken from the training years is then wrong by roughly that gap
 * everywhere at once - which is why the baseline's MAE and RMSE are almost equal.
 */
